{"name":"Melting Snowman","hex":"#dae5e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"melting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Which is melting, dissolving or liquefying.","Given over to strong emotion; tender; aroused; emotional, tearful."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of melt"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/melting"},{"term":"snowman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A humanoid figure made with large snowballs stacked on each other. Human traits like a face and arms may be fashioned with sticks (arms), a carrot (nose), and stones or coal (eyes, mouth).","A score of eight, especially within one inning (in baseball) or on one hole (in golf, where it is also known as dogballs)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Melting","blocks":[{"text":"Melting, or fusion, is a physical process that results in the phase transition of a substance from a solid to a liquid. This occurs when the internal energy of the solid increases, typically by the application of heat or pressure, which increases the substance's temperature to the melting point. At the melting point, the ordering of ions or molecules in the solid breaks down to a less ordered state, and the solid melts to become a liquid."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Melting_icecubes.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melting","wikidata":"Q106080"},{"title":"Snowman","blocks":[{"text":"A snowman is an anthropomorphic snow sculpture often built in regions with sufficient snowfall and is a very common winter tradition. In many places, typical snowmen consist of three large snowballs of different sizes with some additional accoutrements for facial and other features. Due to the sculptability of snow, there is also a wide variety of other styles. Common accessories include branches for arms and a smiling face made of stones, with a carrot used for a nose. Clothing, such as a hat or scarf, may be included."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Snowman_in_Indiana_2014.jpg/330px-Snowman_in_Indiana_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowman","wikidata":"Q483985"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG/250px-BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG/500px-BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG/250px-BoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoiseSnowFamily8249.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg/250px-Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg/500px-Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg/250px-Snowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnowman_on_frozen_lake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Self_portrait_in_snow_-_geograph.org.uk_-_648877.jpg/250px-Self_portrait_in_snow_-_geograph.org.uk_-_648877.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.